    "note": "Substitute House Bill (Comm Sub), HTML with marks; large file read around gun hits. Sec. 1 also changes 'any firearm or other dangerous weapon' to 'all firearms and other dangerous weapons', and the standard cross-references (26.26B.020 replaces 26.26.130). Secs. 4-18 insert 'In issuing the order, the court shall consider the provisions of RCW 9.41.800, and shall order the respondent to surrender ... all firearms, dangerous weapons, and any concealed pistol license' into each protection-order statute (not individually quoted)."
  },
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.800): (1)(a) Require the party immediately to surrender all firearms and other dangerous weapons;\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.800): (1)(b) Require the party to immediately surrender any concealed pistol license issued under RCW  9.41.070;\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.800): (1)(c) Prohibit the party from accessing, obtaining, or possessing any firearms or other dangerous weapons;\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.800): (8) If the court enters a protection order, restraining order, or no-contact order that includes an order to surrender firearms, dangerous weapons, and any concealed pistol license under this section, the order must be served by a law enforcement officer.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new RCW section, chapter 9.41): (2) At the time of surrender, a law enforcement officer taking possession of firearms, dangerous weapons, and any concealed pistol license shall issue a receipt identifying all firearms, dangerous weapons, and any concealed pistol license that have been surrendered and provide a copy of the receipt to the respondent.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new RCW section, chapter 9.41): (3) Upon the sworn statement or testimony of the petitioner or of any law enforcement officer alleging that the respondent has failed to comply with the surrender of firearms or dangerous weapons as required by an order issued under RCW  9.41.800, the court shall determine whether probable cause exists to believe that the respondent has failed to surrender all firearms and dangerous weapons in his or her possession, custody, or control.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new RCW section, chapter 9.41): (5) Upon the issuance of a protection order, no-contact order, or restraining order that includes an order to surrender weapons under RCW  9.41.800, the court shall order a new hearing date and require the respondent to appear not later than three judicial days from the issuance of the order.\nSec. 3 (RCW 9.41.040): (II) Includes an order under RCW  9.41.800 requiring the person to surrender all firearms and prohibiting the person from accessing, obtaining, or possessing firearms;\nNEW SECTION Sec. 19 (repeal): (1) RCW  9.41.802 (Proof of surrender and receipt pattern form—Declaration of nonsurrender pattern form—Administrative office of the courts to develop) and 2014 c 111 s 4; and (2) RCW  9.41.810 (Penalty) and 1984 c 258 s 312, 1983 c 232 s 11, 1983 c 3 s 7, 1961 c 124 s 12, & 1935 c 172 s 16."
